      "value": "@{5c1475afb7ce126e9e0e3a39|full_name}: Of course, it could even actually be UTC ordinal date, that's no problem. (and I would prefer that since I can just make a second clock on my OS) \nBut I'm talking more something that is agreed on by the developers and displayed in various places on the service that can be solidly referenced by anyone for non-programmatic things, as an in game watch on the quick menu: because various countries on earth have \"daylight time\" that varies on it's start date and changes conversions from place to place. For example, it's currently 3AM TOMORROW in japan relative to my time, and that's just plain confusing when trying to figure out when to meet people from JST, PDT, GMT and EDT (and then get used to other times during EST, PST). \nIf it's on the website and in game and we can just look and say \"oh it's Day 112, 17:54\" a simple standard like that avoids all confusion and makes event posts for a global game a lot simpler.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
