        "like": 5
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I want to clarify my aversion to \"just use utc\". Well, yes, but also no. \nIt's actually both i'm advocating for: UTC is the standard to follow, but I want to also encourage the use of current \"day number\" to avoid the confusion around \"Friday\"/\"Saturday\" for example. I experience this every single day due to working with a group that is from PDT/EDT/JST/GMT/CDT all at once and more. \n  \nI've replied with this down below but it's worth putting it up here: \nRight now there's still the issue of \"day of week\" confusing people. it is currently 2am jst Saturday, and 1pm edt Friday. \nIt's 5pm utc \"today\" for me but 5pm utc \"yesterday\" for japan. \nHowever, it's Day 113 17:00 everywhere on earth right now. \nI hope I'm being clear with the distinction here. \nIt's immutable and leaves no room for error, and it's not without precedent, either: final fantasy's mmo's have an internal calendar system with their own standard date that is easy to find, and in game systems that are timed followed it. \nhttps://www.epochconverter.com/daynumbers",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
