      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Swatch has something called Internet Time and the original PSO on Dreamcast used it for their ingame time, where every day was divided into 1000 \"beats\". It was perfect for having a consistent time to tell people when to be online without having to convert timezones.  This was in 2000, don't have to re-invent the wheel.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-04-22T00:01:48.233Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "It would be immensely useful when planning events for there to be a static \"In Universe\" VRChat time and date, ideally in a format like \"time of day\" \"day of year\"  in 24:00/365 format. \nSay for example VRCT: 16:00/210. \nThis time would not adjust for DST, and be accessible from the webpage and on the user UI. \nThis would remove any doubt around event times or time zone conversion.",
